{"level":"error","message":"JSON STRING THAT FAILED TO PARSE: \n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"615c0667-646c-4243-bf6c-97c99ecbcb15\",\n    \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n    \"severity_final\": \"High\",\n    \"justification\": \"The Dockerfile explicitly sets 'USER root'. Running as root increases the risk of container escape and provides an attacker with full privileges within the container environment if an application-level vulnerability (like the command injection found in app.py) is exploited. Most official Node images include a non-privileged 'node' user that should be used instead.\",\n    \"existing_mitigations\": \"None. The Dockerfile explicitly overrides any potential base image defaults to ensure root execution.\",\n    \"patch\": {\n      \"description\": \"Switch to a non-root user. Official Node images provide a 'node' user. We must also ensure the application directory is owned by this user before switching.\",\n      \"code_before\": \"USER root\\n\\n# Copy application files\\nCOPY . /app\\nWORKDIR /app\",\n      \"code_after\": \"WORKDIR /app\\nCOPY --chown=node:node . /app\\nUSER node\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"cc99f0f1-1061-4b62-b2f2-4993f8dfca0f\",\n    \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n    \"severity_final\": \"Medium\",\n    \"justification\": \"Exposing port 22 suggests an intent to run an SSH daemon within the container, which is an anti-pattern for containerized applications. Container management should be handled via orchestrator exec commands (e.g., 'docker exec' or 'kubectl exec'). Exposing this port increases the attack surface for brute-force or credential-based access.\",\n    \"existing_mitigations\": \"The port is only 'exposed' in metadata; it still requires host-level mapping to be reachable from outside the host, but it signals a configuration error.\",\n    \"patch\": {\n      \"description\": \"Remove the EXPOSE 22 instruction. If the application requires a port, expose the specific application port (e.g., 3000 for Node.js).\",\n      \"code_before\": \"EXPOSE 22\",\n      \"code_after\": \"EXPOSE 3000\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"2f5ad4b4-0225-4e6e-99ca-438248e56b70\",\n    \"verdict\": \"confirmed-downgraded\",\n    \"severity_final\": \"Low\",\n    \"justification\": \"While a HEALTHCHECK is a best practice for container orchestration and availability, its absence is not a direct security vulnerability. It is an operational deficiency that could indirectly affect availability (DoS resilience).\",\n    \"existing_mitigations\": \"Orchestrators like Kubernetes may provide their own liveness/readiness probes, making the Dockerfile-level HEALTHCHECK redundant in some deployment contexts.\",\n    \"patch\": {\n      \"description\": \"Add a HEALTHCHECK instruction to monitor the application's health.\",\n      \"code_before\": \"CMD [\\\"node\\\", \\\"index.js\\\"]\",\n      \"code_after\": \"HEALTHCHECK --interval=30s --timeout=3s \\\\\\n  CMD curl -f http:\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"55111461-bead-4efc-96d9-96a00fe7e470\",\n    \"verdict\": \"confirmed\",\n    \"severity_final\": \"Critical\",\n    \"justification\": \"The Dockerfile contains a hardcoded 'API_KEY' in the ENV instruction. Furthermore, the 'COPY . /app' command pulls the '.env' file (which contains AWS_KEY, STRIPE_TOKEN, and GITHUB_TOKEN) into the image layers. These secrets are baked into the image and can be retrieved by anyone with access to the image, even if the container is not running.\",\n    \"existing_mitigations\": \"None. The use of COPY . without a .dockerignore file ensures all local secrets are leaked into the image.\",\n    \"patch\": {\n      \"description\": \"Remove hardcoded environment variables and ensure secrets are not copied into the image. Use a .dockerignore file to exclude .env files and use runtime secret injection (e.g., K8s Secrets, AWS Secret Manager).\",\n      \"code_before\": \"COPY . /app\\n# ...\\nENV API_KEY=\\\"super-secret-key-12345\\\"\",\n      \"code_after\": \"# 1. Create a .dockerignore file containing '.env'\\n# 2. Update Dockerfile:\\nCOPY package*.json ./ \\nRUN npm install\\nCOPY . .\\n# Remove ENV API_KEY line\"\n    }\n  }\n]\n","timestamp":"2026-05-03 14:20:26"}
